// Adversarial stress: Greed protocol under sustained chaos input — Scatter layout.
//
// Greed's 3-system pipeline: greed_on_skip (Update, ungated, reads
// ChipOfferSkipped messages, increments GreedStacks.skips),
// apply_greed_boost (called in-band from generate_chip_offerings, re-weights
// the rarity map), and reset_run_state (clears GreedStacks at run end).
// This stress scenario targets four failure paths:
//
//   1. In-body ActiveProtocols gate — reader leak path: greed_on_skip runs
//      in Update every tick, gated in-body rather than via run_if. When Greed
//      is NOT in ActiveProtocols (before InjectProtocol fires at frame 10 or
//      after a node reset clears the resource), the system must call
//      reader.clear() and return. If the early-return branch is missing or
//      mis-gated, ChipOfferSkipped messages buffer for 10 frames (and again on
//      each node restart), then all replay when Greed becomes active — each
//      replay adding a spurious skip. Scatter layout with chaos input
//      generates chip-select events probabilistically; NoEntityLeaks catches
//      message entity accumulation if the reader drain is skipped.
//
//   2. GreedStacks::skips overflow under extreme chaos: saturating_add
//      prevents wrapping, but chaos input with allow_early_end: false drives
//      sustained chip-select screens across node restarts. If the stack is NOT
//      cleared by reset_run_state (e.g., if GreedStacks is re-inserted rather
//      than init_resource-restored), skips compound run-over-run. The rarity
//      re-weight formula clamps at common_floor = common_original * 0.10, so
//      an enormous skip count drives Common to its floor and concentrates all
//      boost weight on Uncommon/Rare. apply_greed_boost guards boost <= 0.0
//      and uses entry().and_modify (no spurious insert for missing tiers), but
//      the resulting rarity map weights may hit 0.0 or negative if the floor
//      calculation underflows. NoNaN catches NaN in rarity weight arithmetic.
//
//   3. Update vs FixedUpdate scheduling boundary: greed_on_skip runs in
//      Update; the scenario runner's FixedUpdate chaos input fires in
//      FixedUpdate. ChipOfferSkipped messages are written by chip-select
//      systems (also Update). With allow_early_end: false and rapid node
//      cycling, there is a window where a node ends mid-Update before
//      greed_on_skip has processed the final batch of ChipOfferSkipped
//      messages for that node. If reset_run_state (which clears GreedStacks)
//      races with greed_on_skip on the same frame, either:
//        a. greed_on_skip reads skips from the dying run and increments — then
//           reset clears the increment (correct but fragile),
//        b. reset runs first, greed_on_skip increments the fresh zero — the
//           new run starts with skips > 0 (incorrect cross-node state leak).
//      BreakerInBounds and BoltSpeedAccurate catch downstream corruption if
//      rarity state drives invalid chip selection (which could trigger effects
//      that mutate bolt physics in edge-case ways).
//
//   4. apply_greed_boost entry().and_modify semantic: the function only
//      modifies Uncommon/Rare entries that already exist in the rarity map;
//      missing tiers are silently skipped. In layouts where a node's chip
//      offering omits Uncommon or Rare (possible under Scatter with very few
//      cells), all removed weight from Common is added to non-existent entries
//      and silently lost — the total weight sum shrinks. A shrunken weight sum
//      doesn't cause a NaN (it drives selection toward whichever tiers remain)
//      but it can drive the Common weight to exactly its floor with the removed
//      weight vanishing, which is semantically wrong. NoNaN catches any case
//      where weight arithmetic produces NaN; BoltCountReasonable catches
//      downstream chip-effect corruption if a broken rarity selection triggers
//      an effect that spawns or destroys bolts incorrectly.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false sustains pressure across node
// restarts and chip-select screens. 16 runs explore diverse Scatter cell
// arrangements and chip-offer timing distributions.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
        GreedStacksOrphaned,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 4491,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "Greed")),
    ],
)
